# 12. EMPLOYEE MANAGEMENT

Create an employee management module.

Employee fields should include:

```text
Employee ID
First Name
Last Name
Email
Phone
Date of Birth
Joining Date
Department
Designation
Manager
Branch
Location
Employment Type
Status
Profile Photo
Address
Emergency Contact
Bank Details
Documents
```

Do not unnecessarily collect sensitive information unless required.

Employee profile should have tabs:

```text
Overview
Attendance
Leave
Documents
Payroll
Activity
```

---

# 13. ATTENDANCE ENGINE

Attendance is the core module.

Support:

```text
Check In
Check Out
Break Start
Break End
Multiple Punches
Late Arrival
Early Departure
Half Day
Full Day
Absent
Present
Holiday
Leave
Overtime
Work From Home
```

Attendance should be configurable per company.

Do not hard-code attendance rules.

---

# 14. ATTENDANCE FLOW

Basic flow:

```text
Employee
    ↓
Check In
    ↓
Validate User
    ↓
Validate Tenant
    ↓
Validate Shift
    ↓
Validate Location
    ↓
Validate Geofence
    ↓
Optional Selfie Verification
    ↓
Create Attendance Punch
    ↓
Calculate Attendance Status
    ↓
Store Audit Information
```

Record useful metadata such as:

```text
timestamp
IP address
device information
browser
latitude
longitude
location accuracy
attendance method
```

Do not collect unnecessary personal data.

---

# 15. GPS AND GEOFENCING

Support office locations.

Each location should have:

```text
Location Name
Latitude
Longitude
Allowed Radius
Status
```

Example:

```text
Office
Latitude: xx.xxxxx
Longitude: xx.xxxxx
Radius: 200 meters
```

When an employee checks in:

```text
Employee GPS
      ↓
Calculate distance
      ↓
Inside allowed radius?
      ↓
YES → Continue
NO  → Reject or require configured exception
```

Make geofencing configurable.

---

# 16. SELFIE ATTENDANCE

Design the architecture to support selfie-based attendance.

Possible flow:

```text
Camera
 ↓
Capture Image
 ↓
Face Detection
 ↓
Optional Face Verification
 ↓
Attendance
```

The implementation must consider privacy, security, consent, storage, retention, and applicable laws.

Do not claim biometric verification is secure merely because an image was captured.

Prevent obvious spoofing where feasible.

---

# 17. ATTENDANCE REGULARIZATION

Employees should be able to request attendance corrections.

Example:

```text
Date:
31-Aug-2026

Requested Check-In:
09:30 AM

Requested Check-Out:
06:30 PM

Reason:
Forgot to check in
```

Manager/HR can:

```text
Approve
Reject
Request clarification
```

Maintain complete audit history.

---

# 18. SHIFT MANAGEMENT

Support:

```text
Fixed Shift
Flexible Shift
Rotational Shift
Night Shift
Overnight Shift
Split Shift
```

Shift configuration:

```text
Shift Name
Start Time
End Time
Grace Period
Break Duration
Late Threshold
Early Departure Threshold
Overtime Rules
Working Days
```

Support overnight shifts correctly.

Example:

```text
10:00 PM → 06:00 AM
```

Do not incorrectly treat the end time as occurring on the same calendar date.

---

# 19. LEAVE MANAGEMENT

Create:

```text
Leave Types
Leave Balances
Leave Requests
Leave Approval
Leave Calendar
Holiday Calendar
Comp Off
```

Support configurable approval workflows.

Example:

```text
Employee
   ↓
Manager
   ↓
HR
```

---

# 20. HOLIDAY MANAGEMENT

Support:

* Company holidays
* Branch holidays
* Optional holidays
* Regional holidays
* Holiday calendars

Allow administrators to configure holidays by year.

---

# 21. OVERTIME

Track:

```text
Regular Hours
Overtime Hours
Approved Overtime
Rejected Overtime
Overtime Rate
```

Do not automatically pay overtime without configurable business rules and approval.

---

# 22. PAYROLL PREPARATION

Create an architecture that can support payroll.

Attendance should produce:

```text
Working Days
Present Days
Absent Days
Leave Days
LOP Days
Overtime Hours
Late Counts
Early Departure
```

Payroll calculations should be configurable.

Do not hard-code Indian payroll rules unless explicitly required.

Design the system so payroll rules can evolve.

---

# 23. REPORTING

Create professional reports:

```text
Daily Attendance
Monthly Attendance
Employee Attendance
Department Attendance
Late Report
Absent Report
Leave Report
Overtime Report
Regularization Report
Shift Report
Location Report
Payroll Summary
```

Support:

```text
Excel
CSV
PDF
```

Large reports should be generated asynchronously using Celery.

---

# 24. NOTIFICATIONS

Support:

```text
In-App
Email
Push Notification
SMS/WhatsApp integration architecture
```

Examples:

```text
You forgot to check out.

Your leave request was approved.

Your attendance correction was rejected.

You have a pending approval.
```

Create a notification service instead of embedding notification logic into every module.

---

# 25. AUDIT LOG

Every important administrative action should be recorded.

Example:

```text
User:
HR Admin

Action:
Updated Attendance

Employee:
EMP1024

Old Value:
Absent

New Value:
Present

Timestamp:
31-Aug-2026 10:32 AM
```

Audit logs should be append-oriented and protected from normal user modification.

---

# 26. API-FIRST DESIGN

All important functionality should be exposed through clean REST APIs.

Example:

```text
/api/v1/auth
/api/v1/employees
/api/v1/departments
/api/v1/attendance
/api/v1/shifts
/api/v1/leaves
/api/v1/holidays
/api/v1/overtime
/api/v1/reports
/api/v1/notifications
```

Use versioning:

```text
/api/v1/
```

Use proper HTTP status codes.

Use consistent API response structures.

Document APIs automatically through FastAPI/OpenAPI.

---

# 27. API RESPONSE STANDARD

Use a consistent response format.

Success example:

```json
{
  "success": true,
  "message": "Employee created successfully",
  "data": {}
}
```

Error example:

```json
{
  "success": false,
  "message": "Employee not found",
  "error_code": "EMPLOYEE_NOT_FOUND"
}
```

Do not leak internal stack traces to clients.

