# 45. AI HR ASSISTANT FUTURE DESIGN

The architecture should eventually support queries like:

```text
"Who was absent more than 3 days last month?"

"Which employees have frequent late arrivals?"

"Show employees with more than 10 hours overtime."

"Which department has the highest absenteeism?"

"Generate a monthly attendance summary."
```

The AI must respect:

* Tenant isolation
* User permissions
* Data privacy
* Audit requirements

Never allow the AI to bypass authorization.

---

# 46. PERFORMANCE

Design for scalability.

Avoid:

```text
N+1 queries
Large unpaginated queries
Repeated database calls
Blocking HTTP requests
Unnecessary frontend API calls
```

Use:

```text
Pagination
Caching
Indexes
Async/background jobs
Database optimization
Connection pooling
```

---

# 47. DATABASE INDEXING

Identify frequently queried fields and create appropriate indexes.

Examples:

```text
tenant_id
employee_id
attendance_date
department_id
branch_id
status
created_at
```

Do not blindly index every column.

---

# 48. DATA RETENTION

Create configurable retention policies for:

```text
Attendance records
Audit logs
Notifications
Uploaded documents
Selfie images
Location records
```

Do not retain sensitive information forever without a business/legal reason.

---

# 49. SUBSCRIPTION / SaaS BILLING

Eventually support:

```text
Free
Starter
Professional
Enterprise
```

Possible limits:

```text
Employees
Storage
Reports
API calls
Locations
Admin users
Features
```

Implement feature flags/entitlements rather than hard-coding plan checks throughout the application.

